WEBVTT

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.880
Today I thought we'd do an almighty barn.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.880
And I'm gonna ask them to graphically run the colors

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.380
across the screen, so in case you missed them

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.980
in one of our earlier shows, you can pick them up now.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.250
And thought today we'd do what they call

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:44.550
a Wisconsin-Swedish barn.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.650
Now, that's just a big ol' huge barn,

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:49.450
so let's get to going here and let's do one.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:52.980
Gonna start out with a little tiny bit of phthalo blue,

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.980
just a small amount on the large brush,

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:58.110
and we'll drop in a happy little sky here.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:00.000
Starting right at the very top,

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:02.990
going all the way across.

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:06.690
There we are.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:08.970
And we already had the canvas covered with Magic White,

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:12.150
so it's nice and wet and slick and ready to go.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:15.130
And you can see how it's blending with this color.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:18.460
As you work down the canvas, it picks up the Magic White,

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.380
and automatically your color gets lighter

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:24.730
as it gets closer toward the horizon.

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:26.950
Okay, that'll give us a quick little sky,

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:29.120
something to play with.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:30.000
Maybe while it takes,

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:31.720
the phthalo blue and add a little bit

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:35.060
of Van Dyke brown to it, just to dull it down.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.280
And let's go right in here.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.820
Maybe will there be a little bit of water down here?

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:45.770
Just a tiny bit.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:50.740
Okay, that'll give us something to work with.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:55.040
Alright, let's clean the brush.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.240
There we are.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.800
Okay, let's take a one-inch brush

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:05.860
and put some clouds right up here in the sky.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:08.400
I'm gonna take titanium white

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.860
and the smallest, smallest little amount of permanent red

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.080
and just put a little sunshine in the cloud.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:15.620
We don't want to set these clouds on fire.

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:18.840
All we want to do is put a small amount of pink,

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.560
just a little bit.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:21.980
Okay, let's go right up here.

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:23.960
Now, all we do is touch the canvas

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:26.470
and make little tiny circles.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:30.000
And just draw in some basic cloud shapes.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.110
Really push that paint.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:34.940
Keep the brush moving, don't let it set.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.220
Don't want to have big cotton balls up in the sky here.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:40.370
We want to have some nice fluffy little clouds.

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:44.520
And let's go right over here and give him a little friend.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.290
There he is.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:51.710
Just a little floater.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:53.590
Maybe I'll put a tiny bit more right here.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.990
Might make this cloud even larger.

00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:58.090
Now let's take the large brush

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:00.000
and very carefully, very gently,

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.110
just blend the bottom of the clouds out.

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:04.770
This is just a super simple little way

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:07.930
of making clouds that are very effective, very pretty.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:10.070
Only takes you a second.

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:16.130
Now we'll fluff the clouds up, zoop, zoop, there we go.

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:20.430
And very gently, just blend them together.

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:22.070
Isn't that fantastic?

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:26.100
That's such a nice way to make little clouds.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.790
And that gives us a quick little sky.

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:30.000
Now I'm gonna go right into a little

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.330
bit more of the phthalo blue, and alizarin crimson.

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:36.870
We'll just mix it right here on the brush, no big deal.

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:39.640
Looking for a purplish color.

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:41.650
And let's put some little background trees back here.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:43.850
All we're gonna do is just touch the canvas,

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:46.250
pull downward with a large brush.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:49.300
These are just far away little distant trees,

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:56.110
just to give us a little background.

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:58.480
Okay, maybe there's a few right in here.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:06.790
drop them in, wherever you think they ought to be.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:11.220
Okay, now we can clean the brush up again.

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:19.260
We can start painting here.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:22.400
Now then, let's take a one-inch brush

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.240
and begin putting a little highlight

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.000
on some of these distant trees back here.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.000
I'll use a little yellow, yellow ochre.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.370
tiniest little bit of permanent red.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:36.810
Just mix all these colors on the brush.

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.870
And we'll go right back in here

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:41.110
and just drop some basic little colors here and there.

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:43.830
We're not worried about shape in here.

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:52.180
We just want some color in the background.

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:58.060
Just some little things happening far, far away.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.090
There's a nice one.

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:05.120
is just let them fall right off your brush.

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:07.180
Once again, we're not looking for a great deal of detail.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:09.580
This is too far away.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:11.790
Just want some background.

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:16.140
Maybe there's a little right in here.

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:18.860
There's one.

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:21.230
And leave some of these unpainted.

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:22.290
Don't put any highlight on them.

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:25.730
It makes it look like trees that are really, really far away.

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:26.760
Even more distant.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:37.440
Now then, let's take the large brush,

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:41.840
and very gently, I'm just gonna start lifting up.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.490
Very, very gently.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:50.640
Gonna add a small, small amount of the cad yellow here,

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:52.460
just so it mixes with this purplish color

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:58.620
that we have underneath.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:00.000
Just lift up.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.320
make it look like maybe a little hill

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:08.750
that's far, far away.

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:11.420
Isn't that fantastic that you could

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:13.380
make a background that quick?

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:16.360
I used to work for weeks to make a background,

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:20.330
and even longer to do the painting.

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:24.780
Okay, let's jump in here and start us a barn.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:27.070
Now, if you were with us on previous shows,

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:30.000
we've decided it's quite helpful if we take

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.040
we can scrape out a basic shape,

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:34.220
and it gets rid of the loose, thin paint off the canvas,

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:36.180
and we can put our firm paint back on,

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:37.560
and really take off.

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:39.460
So let's decide where the old barn's gonna be,

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:43.240
and as I say, this is gonna be a big, huge barn.

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:47.420
Maybe right here, like so.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:50.470
And just put in a basic shape.

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:54.610
This is a super way just to lay out your ideas

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:57.260
without really committing yourself.

00:06:57.260 --> 00:07:00.000
Maybe it comes down like that, and then out.

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:03.990
There we go.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:10.710
Just take that loose paint right off the canvas.

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:17.090
Firm paint back on, it'll be right against the fabric.

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:20.890
It'll really give us something to work with.

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:23.080
Okay, Van Dyke Brown.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:25.730
Let's go right into the Van Dyke Brown.

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:28.230
Begin blocking in this basic bar.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:35.550
Just straight old Van Dyke brown.

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:40.440
Just let the knife do the work.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:46.810
Okay, maybe right down through here.

00:07:46.810 --> 00:07:51.700
And we just fill all this up with brown.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:08:00.000
Only takes you a second one.

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:09.990
using a big ol' knife.

00:08:09.990 --> 00:08:13.790
Give us a nice base color to work with.

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:15.950
Comes right out here like so.

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:25.190
One over here, here, and just fill all this in.

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:27.090
And we're not worried about detail at this time.

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:29.800
All we're doing is laying the base color in.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:34.420
So don't worry about detail.

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:38.280
See, already we have a nice basic barn shape here.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:44.440
There we go.

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:48.300
And now we can begin worrying about little details.

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:50.790
Okay, and we'll take some Van Dyke Brown

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:54.730
and permanent red.

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:57.420
And maybe this old barn has shingles on it,

00:08:57.420 --> 00:08:58.930
so we'll put some shingles.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.740
There we go, that gives us a nice color to work with.

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:08.530
Now, up here we're gonna have some angles

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:10.150
that we just see the edge of the shingle,

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:12.170
so we really don't have to spend a great deal of time

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:14.440
worrying about them here.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:22.090
All we're gonna see is the edges.

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:22.930
Just drop these in.

00:09:22.930 --> 00:09:25.180
All I'm doing is just touching the canvas

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:30.000
and following the angles that we've put into the roof here.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.700
Angles are very, very important.

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:34.140
In this series, we've tried to show you

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:39.580
quite a few buildings, just let you go.

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:43.550
Now then, take a little bit of the titanium white,

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:49.370
a little brown in it, just a small amount of brown,

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:51.570
and let's begin highlighting these little edges.

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:53.570
Maybe there's a little highlight here,

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:58.710
and one that comes right down like so.

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:09.640
we can work on this angle right here.

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:10.890
And I'm gonna take,

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:13.350
let me clean up a spot here to work on.

00:10:13.350 --> 00:10:17.270
Gonna take and mix up some phthalo green

00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:20.120
and alizarin crimson in about equal parts.

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:24.760
Make us a nice gray color.

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:28.800
Very, very dark, very dark.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.120
a little bit of white.

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:38.690
Maybe a touch more of the crimson into that.

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:40.470
That's better, that's what I'm looking for.

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:47.220
A nice gray color.

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:52.160
Okay, let's go right up in here.

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:57.300
Angles, once again, are most, most important.

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:58.840
Just pull it across.

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:05.980
And you can vary that with a little bit of darker color

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:07.780
if you want to push it back a little further,

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:10.490
make it look old.

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:15.780
You need to come right down through here with a highlight.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:21.020
Sun would strike right there, like so.

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:22.480
And now it's time to start figuring out

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:25.700
where the other side of the barn is here.

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:27.440
Before we do that though, we can take a little bit

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:30.000
of the light brown and make it look like little boards

00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:32.850
Pieces of wood.

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:38.370
All we're doing is just touching the canvas.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:39.810
Maybe there's a big door right here

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:44.030
where they load the hay.

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:49.230
Highlight around the door.

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:50.770
Just a little bit of color.

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:54.360
There's some boards here that they made the door out of.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:10.880
just to give us an idea.

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:14.730
And let's make some shingles on this roof.

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:16.110
And just like you were laying shingles,

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:20.090
start at the bottom using the little edge of the knife.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:22.730
Just start laying in some shingles.

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:23.720
Start at the bottom.

00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:32.470
So the bottom of the top one

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:35.450
covers the top of the bottom one.

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:39.770
That's hard to say.

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:43.470
And just do one row at a time.

00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:47.040
These old shingles are all beat up in weather,

00:12:47.040 --> 00:12:52.000
beaten, and they've had a rough life out here.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.540
Follow the angles in your roof.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:58.720
Most, most important.

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:00.000
And this will give it a layer

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:13.660
Keep layering 'til you get all the way to the top.

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:18.110
And at home, when you have all kinds of time,

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:20.290
you can really make some little tiny shingles

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:22.600
and a lot of detail into this.

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:26.870
There, that gives us a nice shingle-looking roof.

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:30.000
Now we have to make some more determination

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.200
Where does this come?

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:33.910
Maybe it comes right out like that.

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:36.260
We'll just put this in and sort of give us

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:37.560
a guide to follow.

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:45.350
Get a little bit more of the brown and permanent red.

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:52.160
Begin laying some shingles right here.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:54.160
Now these are laying down, so you don't see them

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:56.360
at the same angle that you would see these here.

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:59.200
So all you have to do is just touch the canvas.

00:14:00.510 --> 00:14:10.060
Just touch the canvas, there you go.

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:12.680
Isn't that a super way to put a roof on a barn?

00:14:12.680 --> 00:14:17.600
God, I wished it was that easy in real life.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:29.380
Okay, now, let's take blue, Van Dyke Brown,

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:43.090
and a little touch of white.

00:14:43.090 --> 00:14:48.390
I'll just mix it up 'til it's marbled.

00:14:48.390 --> 00:14:51.460
We can begin putting some boards here.

00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:55.220
Maybe from here, right down.

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:56.360
Just let 'em come down.

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:11.330
I want this to be all weather beaten, so.

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:13.770
Let the paint break, let all these little things happen.

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:16.070
Maybe there's a little touch of this color

00:15:16.070 --> 00:15:19.360
right up here, just so it follows through.

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:34.050
We can put in some little boards here

00:15:34.050 --> 00:15:38.780
just by dragging the knife right down through the paint,

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:48.010
like so, wherever you think they should be.

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:49.650
Now this side over here, we want to keep it

00:15:49.650 --> 00:15:53.130
very, very dark, very dark.

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:57.750
So just some little indications.

00:15:57.750 --> 00:16:00.000
Just put a few little indications of a board here

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:04.120
We don't want a lot of detail over here.

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:07.910
Okay, now, we need a door to get in that barn.

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:10.180
Gotta have a way to put the horse in there.

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:12.420
So let's just come right here and maybe,

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:15.940
maybe there's a big door on this barn.

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:17.450
Just like so.

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:21.680
Just pull it across, this is just straight Van Dyke brown.

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:23.750
There we go.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:26.440
And we can take a little bit of the light color

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:28.580
and highlight it so that door stands out.

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:34.080
Son of a gun, we got a pretty good looking

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:37.060
ol' barn going here.

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:40.660
Okay, now, clean up a spot on the pallet again

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:42.620
so we can work.

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:46.000
We can begin putting some land around the barn.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:49.340
Straight Van Dyke brown, put a little bit of,

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:53.070
a little bit of burn number into it.

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:56.790
Now we can begin filling all this in.

00:16:56.790 --> 00:16:59.920
Maybe there's an angle like so with the land.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:14.470
This is where we worry about at the bottom of our barn

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:23.700
and begin getting it straight and everything worked out.

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:28.550
Just put the dark in, we need some dirt under there.

00:17:28.550 --> 00:17:30.000
Then we'll plant some grass on it

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:55.030
Okay, maybe right down here, maybe there's a little pond,

00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:57.450
just a small little pond that maybe the farmer

00:17:57.450 --> 00:18:00.000
dug it himself so he'd have

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:03.510
for his cows and horses to get a little drink of water.

00:18:03.510 --> 00:18:06.490
So we'll just pull a little bit of this brown down

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:09.010
and allow that to be our reflection.

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:14.120
Now what's fun is to reflect the whole barn into the water.

00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:20.470
Okay, now gently go across.

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:23.240
Okay, now we can take our fan brush

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:26.360
and start putting some little grassy areas in here.

00:18:26.360 --> 00:18:28.550
We'll use some cad yellow.

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:31.590
A little bit of yellow ochre.

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:32.890
A little touch of permanent red.

00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:34.880
Just mix these on the brush.

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:37.130
And some sap green.

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:40.660
And let these colors mix in the brush

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:42.700
and that way you have a multitude of things happening

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:43.640
right here in the brush.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:44.940
You don't have to spend a lot of time

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:47.420
trying to mix all these different colors.

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:50.100
Touch, push upward.

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:52.090
Make all those little grassy things

00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:54.000
just sort of happen there.

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:56.630
And do it in layers,

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:58.450
starting from the area that's farthest away

00:18:58.450 --> 00:18:59.540
and work forward.

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:04.150
Just do it in layers.

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:09.070
And this is the way you create the contour of the land.

00:19:09.070 --> 00:19:10.290
And let's see now.

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:12.500
Got some grass up there.

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:16.540
So let's put, maybe there's a happy little road here.

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:20.980
Little place where they go into the barn.

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:25.720
Comes, just drop it in.

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:29.080
This is just Van Dyke brown and burnt umber.

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:30.000
And then we'll go back.

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.960
with a little brown and white.

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:38.300
And we can lay a tiny little bit of highlight on here.

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:39.900
There, we don't know where that road goes.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:44.000
It just disappears.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:48.890
There we go.

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:51.810
Now we can begin putting some grass

00:19:51.810 --> 00:19:53.250
on the other side of the road.

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:57.460
Just drop it in, using the old fan brush here.

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:13.640
Doesn't it look like an old barn yet?

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:15.450
I like to do old buildings.

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:18.040
I think they're just fantastic.

00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:19.740
Spend a lot of time with the camera

00:20:19.740 --> 00:20:21.780
taking pictures of old buildings for ideas

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:25.480
as we travel around the country.

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:28.710
Let's take a little brown and white here.

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:33.440
and maybe there's a little highlight that shows right here,

00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:41.560
so we'll just put a little bit here and there.

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:44.400
There's a million things around you every day to paint.

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:47.210
Just look around and notice 'em.

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:50.260
That's all it takes.

00:20:50.260 --> 00:20:52.180
They're always present.

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:53.780
We see 'em so often, we have a tendency

00:20:53.780 --> 00:20:56.170
just to overlook 'em.

00:20:56.170 --> 00:21:00.000
So take the time to look at 'em.

00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:03.880
Fantastic, but you just have to spend a little time

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:07.130
appreciating it, studying it.

00:21:07.130 --> 00:21:14.760
There's a beauty in every tree, in every bush.

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:19.600
Just put a little water line around there.

00:21:19.600 --> 00:21:23.870
Pipples in the water.

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:26.370
There's a little water line right there.

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:28.870
Wherever you want 'em, this is your world.

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:32.150
Okay, now we got a whole right side here

00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:34.710
we have to do something with.

00:21:34.710 --> 00:21:38.530
So, let's take, let's take

00:21:38.530 --> 00:21:40.690
a little bit of Sap Green,

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:42.500
Alizarin Crimson, Van Dyke Brown.

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:44.810
We just mix it together on the brush here.

00:21:44.810 --> 00:21:47.610
And let's go right up in here

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:49.110
and take the big brush

00:21:49.110 --> 00:21:50.690
and let's just push a happy little tree

00:21:50.690 --> 00:21:57.890
right out of the brush it goes.

00:21:57.890 --> 00:21:59.830
Just let it...

00:22:04.060 --> 00:22:05.600
What started out as a happy little tree

00:22:05.600 --> 00:22:08.200
ends up as a happy big tree.

00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:10.980
And some little things right in here.

00:22:10.980 --> 00:22:13.180
Wherever, wherever.

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:21.630
Just let your heart take you wherever you wanna go.

00:22:21.630 --> 00:22:24.790
Maybe this just comes right down like so.

00:22:24.790 --> 00:22:29.540
I just fill all this up with some nice dark color.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:31.670
in order to show light.

00:22:31.670 --> 00:22:38.510
You know, just looking at my barn here,

00:22:38.510 --> 00:22:41.780
we ought to have a wheel to pull the hay up.

00:22:41.780 --> 00:22:45.240
So I'll take a little bit of paint thinner

00:22:45.240 --> 00:22:46.980
and thin down my Van Dyke Brown

00:22:46.980 --> 00:22:49.430
until it's almost like water on the liner brush.

00:22:49.430 --> 00:22:52.010
Bring it to a nice, sharp point.

00:22:52.010 --> 00:22:53.690
And let's go right up here.

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:55.620
Maybe an old wheel up here.

00:22:55.620 --> 00:22:59.480
Just go around, like so.

00:23:00.990 --> 00:23:03.640
put some spokes in that wheel.

00:23:03.640 --> 00:23:05.740
This is so they can pull the hay up

00:23:05.740 --> 00:23:07.690
and put it up in the barn.

00:23:07.690 --> 00:23:09.010
So when it gets colder,

00:23:09.010 --> 00:23:12.110
the old cow's got a little something to eat.

00:23:12.110 --> 00:23:13.950
The little stick that comes out here

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:16.920
that holds that wheel.

00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:22.090
Okay, let's take a little bit of Van Dyke Brown.

00:23:22.090 --> 00:23:25.220
Little white on one side.

00:23:25.220 --> 00:23:28.620
Very quickly, drop in a couple little trunks here.

00:23:28.620 --> 00:23:29.410
There he goes.

00:23:31.790 --> 00:23:34.480
friend right there.

00:23:34.480 --> 00:23:38.710
All righty, now we can take the one-inch brush.

00:23:38.710 --> 00:23:44.060
We'll use a little bit of cad yellow and sap green.

00:23:44.060 --> 00:23:45.500
And let's begin highlighting some of these

00:23:45.500 --> 00:23:49.320
beautiful little things back here.

00:23:49.320 --> 00:23:55.260
Just drop 'em in.

00:23:55.260 --> 00:24:00.000
There's a nice one, there's a nice one.

00:24:03.450 --> 00:24:08.180
There's one right there.

00:24:08.180 --> 00:24:16.850
Just drop these little rascals wherever you want them.

00:24:16.850 --> 00:24:21.470
Put some up here on this big tree.

00:24:21.470 --> 00:24:29.100
This is just cad yellow, a little bit of sap green.

00:24:29.100 --> 00:24:30.000
Just drop the rascals

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:32.130
any of where you want them.

00:24:32.130 --> 00:24:43.120
Get your imagination, just go free.

00:24:43.120 --> 00:24:45.720
Okay, now maybe the old farmer

00:24:45.720 --> 00:24:48.150
had him a little fence out here,

00:24:48.150 --> 00:24:50.090
so let's just drop a happy little fence in.

00:24:50.090 --> 00:24:52.640
We'll put a few little posts here.

00:24:52.640 --> 00:24:59.600
There they go, there.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:05.470
one that we just barely can see.

00:25:05.470 --> 00:25:08.970
Touch a little highlight to 'em, bloop.

00:25:08.970 --> 00:25:10.800
Don't want a great deal, just a little.

00:25:10.800 --> 00:25:14.700
Just to make 'em stand out.

00:25:14.700 --> 00:25:16.530
A little magic white on the knife,

00:25:16.530 --> 00:25:22.790
and put some wire on that fence.

00:25:22.790 --> 00:25:25.780
Three strands there.

00:25:25.780 --> 00:25:28.390
Okay, now we can finish this rascal up.

00:25:31.370 --> 00:25:33.890
and drop in some other little bush.

00:25:33.890 --> 00:25:35.690
If you're gonna be painting along with us next week,

00:25:35.690 --> 00:25:36.890
we'll be doing a white canvas,

00:25:36.890 --> 00:25:39.960
so you can have your easel set up all ready to go.

00:25:39.960 --> 00:25:42.540
Paint along with us.

00:25:42.540 --> 00:25:43.580
Let's take a little bit of brown.

00:25:43.580 --> 00:25:46.440
I'm getting crazy here, we're out of time.

00:25:46.440 --> 00:25:47.240
But we'll do it anyway.

00:25:47.240 --> 00:25:50.790
I'm gonna put a little path right here.

00:25:50.790 --> 00:25:54.710
A little path, so we can walk around.

00:25:54.710 --> 00:25:57.510
Just Van Dyke brown.

00:25:57.510 --> 00:25:59.350
Let it mix with the color it's underneath.

00:26:00.730 --> 00:26:03.850
Just like so.

00:26:03.850 --> 00:26:06.460
And we'll take a little bit of brown and white,

00:26:06.460 --> 00:26:11.450
put some highlight on here.

00:26:11.450 --> 00:26:15.300
There we are, give us a little path.

00:26:15.300 --> 00:26:18.200
Then we'll put a few little bushes right over here,

00:26:18.200 --> 00:26:25.980
just to close that path in.

00:26:25.980 --> 00:26:28.960
And I think this one is just about finished.

00:26:28.960 --> 00:26:30.000
We can drop a signature

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:33.090
in here and have a finished painting.

00:26:33.090 --> 00:26:34.430
I hope you've enjoyed this one.

00:26:34.430 --> 00:26:35.630
It's a great deal of fun.

00:26:35.630 --> 00:26:38.420
It will teach you a lot about buildings

00:26:38.420 --> 00:26:41.340
and make your heart happy.

00:26:41.340 --> 00:26:43.880
Let's sign on the right side this time.

00:26:43.880 --> 00:26:46.210
I'll drop a quick signature in here.

00:26:46.210 --> 00:26:48.110
I'd like to wish each and every one of you

00:26:48.110 --> 00:26:52.060
happy painting, God bless,

00:26:52.060 --> 00:26:54.340
and we'll see you next week.

00:26:54.340 --> 00:26:57.720
Bye-bye.
